# Series entries we skip on THIS base, each with a reason. The importer never
# touches this file, so the reasons survive a refresh.

# CVE-2017-9118: its hunk 2 deletes an OLD `#define ZSTR_MAX_LEN` that only exists
# in CloudLinux's newer base — pristine 7.3.33 has no ZSTR_MAX_LEN at all, so that
# hunk rejects. We keep the fix via patches-local/73/php-7.3-CVE-2017-9118.patch
# (hunk 1 that ADDS ZSTR_MAX_OVERHEAD + ZSTR_MAX_LEN, plus both ext/pcre hunks);
# only the no-op deletion is dropped. CVE-2017-8923 / CVE-2024-11236 depend on the
# ZSTR_MAX_LEN definition, so it must stay defined.
php-7.3-CVE-2017-9118.patch

# CVE-2025-1218 (CloudLinux caching_sha2 add-on): its php_mysqlnd_cached_sha2_result_read()
# hunks target alt-php's own caching_sha2 backport; our base has no such function, so
# they reject. The main CVE-2025-1218 patch applies and stays.
php-7.3-CVE-2025-1218-caching-sha2.patch
